<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nehale lyaMpingana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1840s–1908</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Nehale Mpingana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nehale lyaMpingana was ruler of eastern Ondonga, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovambo-people">Ovambo</a> kingdoms of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>, from 1884 until his death in 1908. On 28 January 1904, during the Herero uprising, his warriors attacked the German fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namutoni">Namutoni</a> and forced the small garrison to abandon it. He is honoured in Namibia as a hero of early anti-colonial resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nehale-lyampingana.jpg" alt="Nehale lyaMpingana" width="266" height="364" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suomen Lähetysseura · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nehale_Mpingana.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
